#!RuleTest
#test FDA-CT2001 expect=noViolation domain=DS
#note "SENDIG-AR 1.0 prints no DS; the base-IG view (PLAN-send-base-ig-view, B-BASE) reads it from SENDIG v3.1. Every DSDECOD is a term of the non-extensible DSDECOD codelist -> no finding."
#library-ref standard=sendig version=ar-1-0 ct=sendct-2026-03-27
dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | S1-001 | 1 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | 2020-05-11
S1 | DS | S1-002 | 1 | INTERIM SACRIFICE | INTERIM SACRIFICE | 2020-05-12
---
